:R-HSA-6806667  a           owl:NamedIndividual , obo:GO_0006775 ;
        rdfs:comment        "Vitamins A, D, E, and K are classified as fat-soluble. Metabolic pathways by which dietary precursors of vitamins A (Harrison 2005) and K (Shearer et al. 2012) are converted to active forms are annotated here. The conversion of 7-dehydrocholesterol is converted to active vitamin D (Dusso et al. 2005) is annotated as part of metabolism of steroids. (Vitamin E (tocopherol) is available in active form from the diet.)" ;
        rdfs:label          "Metabolism of fat-soluble vitamins" ;
        dc:contributor      "Edited: D'Eustachio, Peter, 2015-11-02" , "Reviewed: Jassal, Bijay, 2015-11-02" , "GOC:reactome_curators" , "Authored: D'Eustachio, Peter, 2015-11-02" ;
        dc:date             "2023-06-21" ;
